          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The routine is short: <strong class="text-white">cartridge out, bag out, foam sleeve on, stay under the max fill line</strong>. Work the nozzle in contact with the floor rather than sweeping, and let the change in the machine’s note tell you when the float has risen.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Afterwards, <strong class="text-white">drain, rinse, dry the sleeve separately and leave the lid off</strong>. Ten minutes there is the difference between a machine that smells fine in five years and one that announces every wet job it has ever done.
